index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..161eb03d7c493a966103796e3f3cc38052f40d54
--- /dev/null
+++ b/web/AUTOPLAY.md
@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@
+# Host autoplay
+
+Both `@white-label/player-web/shaka` and `/bitmovin` accept:
+
+```ts
+const bridge = createBridge({ autoplay: true }); // Attempts playback with audio, no gesture gate.
+// createBridge({ autoplay: false });           // Waits for Play.
+// createBridge({ autoplay: true, muted: true }); // Explicit silent startup.
+```
+
+Autoplay and mute are independent: autoplay defaults to true in the package,
+and muted defaults to false. No startup path silently mutes audio on rejection.
+The host's content-card/Play click is a genuine interaction; it should open the
+player with `autoplay: true, muted: false`. The player attempts audible startup.
+A browser may still deny it, especially when mounting/loading occurs after the
+original click. In that case the visible player Play button retries directly
+from a new gesture. Do not synthesize clicks or claim to transfer activation.
+The existing volume control can change sound from a user gesture. No code can
+promise playback when a user/browser blocks all autoplay. Shaka catches rejected
+play attempts; Bitmovin's blocked-play warning clears buffering and reports paused.
+
+Shaka initializes IMA immediately for autoplay; false retains Play-bound
+initialization. Every request supplies `setAdWillAutoPlay` and
+`setAdWillPlayMuted`; Shaka propagates the content mute state to IMA. Prerolls
+remain ahead of content, and ads continue to lock content transport.
+
+The React host's `VideoPlayerOverlay` accepts `autoplay` (default false), e.g.
+`<VideoPlayerOverlay autoplay={true} {...otherProps} />`, forwarding it through
+both service adapters. Sync a package built from these player sources for the
+new audio/ad startup behavior. The standalone demo retains its existing startup.
+
+Browser policies checked 2026-11-16:
+- [Chrome](https://developer.chrome.com/blog/autoplay): muted autoplay allowed;
+  audible playback depends on interaction, engagement, or other permission.
+- [WebKit](https://webkit.org/blog/7734/auto-play-policy-changes-for-macos/):
+  detect rejected playback; settings can block silent autoplay as well.
+- [Firefox](https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/block-autoplay): sound blocked
+  by default; users can block both audio and video.
+- [Google IMA](https://developers.google.com/interactive-media-ads/docs/sdks/html5/client-side/autoplay):
+  provide autoplay/mute request flags and preserve click-to-play fallback.
+
+Verification: `node web/tests/autoplay.cjs`, `node web/tests/ad-resume.cjs`,
+typecheck, library and demo builds. A Chrome/macOS fixture using the actual
+Shaka bridge previously verified true/false with and without Google prerolls
+using the earlier muted-start policy. The default-audio correction is covered
+by configuration tests; real audible startup still requires browser QA. Bitmovin
+configuration is simulated; real playback requires a valid license key,
+which is absent in this workspace. Safari/Firefox playback is not observed.
